  "findings": {
    "generators": "Source defines the declared five Frobenius draws100..104, five row draws200..204, within-row permutation300 and elementwise sign flips301. Random ensembles replace Wo as well as recurrent/input weights; readout is unused by prefix gates but affects diagnostic accuracy. No generated bytes, positive-norm assumptions or finite draw law replayed.",
    "prefix": "run uses complete packed gate-history keys distinct from simplex-fan pieces, forwards exact=True recursively, and terminates at k without correctness subdivision. Exact branch still uses floating TOL/rank/clip decisions. No source-to-exact-real completeness certification for new models follows.",
    "mass": "Driver sorts/sums history-keyed numerical mass values and emits aggregate N/inverseSimpson/total only. Reached4D code contains fixed Duffy10 and log-Plackett128, determinant/denominator floors and finite precision. Raw histories/mass values/rays are not saved by rc.py, so threshold minimality, positivity, numerical integration and complete partition cannot be independently audited from these aggregates.",
    "accuracy": "acc regenerates a million10D Gaussian rows with seed7 for each model, first-index argmax and argsort second label. Common streams are source-qualified; saved means are not independent per-model draws or reconstructed forwards. Realized model/checkpoint/runtime bytes and per-observation outcomes absent from driver outputs.",
    "provenance": "All50 payloads and3 reviewer documents match frozen Git bytes/hashes. Preregistration is an ancestor of source/results publication; this does not certify execution chronology, exploratory absence or checkpoint/runtime identity. Local m43 import loads an unrelated frozen NPZ; it was hashed but not decoded here.",
    "selection": "drive.sh processes13 models at k2..4, skips existing files without source-hash validation, and does not run k5. Historical600-second wall timeouts and memory setting differ from current review limits. cpu_total excludes model creation; geometry proxy excludes separate mass counters. No complete-cost or k5 evidence inferred.",
    "grouping": "Preregistered median uses10 random draws, not permutation/sign-flip controls. README prose ranges include control endpoints in places; later reconciliation must keep frob5,row5,random10 and all12 nontarget groups distinct. drive.log begins frob1/k2, so it is partial and missing entries are not fabricated.",
    "interpretation": "Finite within30percent descriptive category is not training-effect equivalence, generic higher-depth equality, architecture ceiling or proof of exponential continuation. Existing T236 proof remains conditional ideal algebra, not a validation of random-model counts or Gaussian masses."
  },
